## Partial Identity Data Is Still Security-Relevant

The last four digits of a Social Security number are not equivalent to exposure of a complete SSN.

That distinction should remain explicit.

However:

`Name + DOB + Address + Phone + Last Four SSN`

can still provide attackers with a substantially stronger identity profile than any field alone.

Attackers increasingly operate across datasets.

One breach may provide:

`Name + Address`

Another:

`Email + Password`

Another:

`DOB + Phone`

Another:

`Last Four SSN`

Combined:

Name
+
Address
+
Email
+
Phone
+
DOB
+
Partial SSN
↓
Higher-confidence identity profile

This is why breach impact cannot always be evaluated in isolation.

