## Detection Opportunities Inside the Cloud Environment

Because ADT has not publicly established the exact initial-access mechanism, defenders should focus on telemetry capable of identifying unauthorized authenticated access regardless of how the identity was obtained.

### Identity Telemetry

Monitor:

* impossible travel
* first-seen IP addresses
* unusual ASN
* atypical geography
* new device sign-ins
* new browser fingerprints
* MFA resets
* MFA method additions
* password resets
* dormant-account activation
* privileged-role changes
* OAuth grants
* unusual service-account behavior
* token anomalies
* helpdesk-assisted authentication changes

### Data-Access Telemetry

Monitor:

* bulk customer searches
* unusually broad queries
* large downloads
* mass record enumeration
* repeated sequential queries
* unusual report generation
* export operations
* API extraction
* access outside normal job function
* historical-record access
* unusually high query volume

### Cloud Telemetry

Depending on platform:

* IAM changes
* console logins
* database queries
* storage access
* API-key creation
* secret retrieval
* token creation
* application registrations
* OAuth consent
* snapshot creation
* export jobs
* cross-region transfer
* logging disablement
* security-policy modifications

