## Questions InfinityGrid Still Wants Answered

* What exact cloud service or application was compromised?
* What was the initial-access mechanism?
* Was social engineering involved?
* Was voice phishing involved?
* Which identity was compromised?
* How did the attacker authenticate?
* Was MFA configured?
* Was MFA reset or manipulated?
* Was an attacker-controlled authentication method added?
* Were session tokens stolen?
* Was OAuth involved?
* Was a privileged account involved?
* Was privilege escalation required?
* How long did unauthorized access persist?
* How quickly did ADT detect the activity?
* What volume of records was accessed?
* Were bulk exports generated?
* Was an API used?
* How was data exfiltrated?
* How many unique individuals were affected?
* How many records contained DOB?
* How many contained partial SSNs?
* How many contained partial Tax IDs?
* How long had prospect records been retained?
* What prevented access to payment information?
* What prevented access to customer security systems?
* Were those systems technically segmented or merely inaccessible to the compromised identity?
* What security controls changed after the incident?
* Has ADT materially changed cloud authorization or identity architecture since the breach?

